# "azgen" = half; in the construct state after the connective "d" it surfaces
# as "wezgen".  kab.wikipedia, Tafsut n Yimaziɣen:
#   "ɣef ṛṛebɛa d wezgen n tmeddit"   (half past four in the evening)
#   "ɣef leḥdac d wezgen n tṣ̣ebḥit"  (half past eleven in the morning)
wezgen
azgen
# Tatoeba Kabyle also writes the construct-state "uzgen" after the connective:
#   "Attan qrib d lweḥda d uzgen." -- "It's almost half past one already."
uzgen
